# Strictly obey rules unless the user changes them

- Treat **all** project rules (`.cursorrules`, `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`, and explicit user instructions in the thread) as binding.
- **Do not** relax, reinterpret, or “balance” rules against convenience, helpfulness, or speed.
- If two rules appear to conflict, apply the **stricter** or more **user-directed** reading; do not pick the one that does more automatically unless the user asked for that.
- **Only** depart from an existing rule when the user **explicitly** says to go back, change, or override that rule for this task or going forward.
- When the user gives a one-off exception, scope it to what they said (this message / this file / this session)—do not assume they revoked a rule permanently unless they say so.
